ncss({ zIndex: 10 }) // fine","lang":"tsx","html":"<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">width</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-string\">&quot;5rem&quot;</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// fine</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">width</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">5</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// error: unitless-length</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">flexGrow</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">1</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// fine - flex-grow takes a number</span>\n<span class=\"th-token th-function\">css</span>({ <span class=\"th-token th-property\">zIndex</span>: <span class=\"th-token th-number\">10</span> }) <span class=\"th-token th-comment\">// fine</span>"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The rule is the CSS rule: a property that takes a "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"&lt;<span class=\"th-token th-tag\">length</span>&gt;","source":"<length>"}},{"type":"text","value":" needs a unit. A\nproperty whose value is a plain number takes a plain number. Guessing "},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"px","source":"px"}},{"type":"text","value":" is how\na styling system ends up with values it cannot explain, so the compiler asks you\ninstead."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Invalid values are errors too ("},{"type":"inlineComponent","name":"inline-code","tagName":"md-inline-code","attributes":{},"children":[],"properties":{"html":"invalid-value","source":"invalid-value"}},{"type":"text","value":"), checked against the property's\ngrammar as MDN writes it:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"code",